{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.StandardModel.BrunnianIsotypeExclusion","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.StandardModel.BrunnianIsotypeExclusion","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.Perm.Sign","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Action.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.RepresentationTheory.Basic"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.piStd_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.piStd_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/BrunnianIsotypeExclusion.lean#L168-L175","doc":"**`π_Std(t) = 0`** for a totally antisymmetric tensor `ρ σ v = sgn(σ)·v`:\n`t − 0 − t = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.piAlt_eq_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.piAlt_eq_self","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/BrunnianIsotypeExclusion.lean#L157-L166","doc":"**`π_Alt(t) = t`** for a totally antisymmetric tensor `ρ σ v = sgn(σ)·v`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.piSym_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.piSym_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/BrunnianIsotypeExclusion.lean#L150-L155","doc":"**`π_Sym(t) = 0`** for a totally antisymmetric tensor `ρ σ v = sgn(σ)·v`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.piStd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.piStd","kind":"def","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/BrunnianIsotypeExclusion.lean#L145-L146","doc":"The standard-isotype projector `π_Std = 1 − π_Sym − π_Alt`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.piAlt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.piAlt","kind":"def","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/BrunnianIsotypeExclusion.lean#L141-L143","doc":"The sign-isotype (alternating) projector `π_Alt = (1/6) Σ_σ sgn(σ)·σ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.piSym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.piSym","kind":"def","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/BrunnianIsotypeExclusion.lean#L138-L139","doc":"The trivial-isotype (symmetric) projector `π_Sym = (1/6) Σ_σ σ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.stdCombination_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.stdCombination_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/BrunnianIsotypeExclusion.lean#L115-L123","doc":"**Standard projection vanishes.** The (scaled) standard combination\n`6 • t − Σ_σ σ • t − Σ_σ sgn(σ) • (σ • t) = 6·π_Std(t)` vanishes for a totally\nantisymmetric tensor: `6•t − 0 − 6•t = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.altSum_eq_card_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.altSum_eq_card_smul","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/BrunnianIsotypeExclusion.lean#L104-L113","doc":"**Alternating projection is the identity.** For a totally antisymmetric\ntensor, the unnormalized signed sum `Σ_σ sgn(σ) • (σ • t) = 6·π_Alt(t)` equals\n`6 • t`, because `sgn(σ)² = 1` collapses every summand to `t`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.symSum_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.symSum_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/BrunnianIsotypeExclusion.lean#L94-L102","doc":"**Symmetric projection vanishes.** For a totally antisymmetric tensor\n`σ • t = sgn(σ) • t`, the unnormalized symmetric sum `Σ_σ σ • t = 6·π_Sym(t)`\nvanishes — the sign identity `Σ sgn σ = 0` kills it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.sign_mul_self_cast","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.sign_mul_self_cast","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/BrunnianIsotypeExclusion.lean#L77-L81","doc":"The cast sign squares to `1` in any ring `R`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.sign_sum_cast_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.sign_sum_cast_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/BrunnianIsotypeExclusion.lean#L71-L75","doc":"The signs sum to zero after casting into any ring `R`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.sign_mul_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.sign_mul_self","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/BrunnianIsotypeExclusion.lean#L65-L69","doc":"Each permutation sign squares to `1`, since `sgn σ = ±1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.sign_sum_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.sign_sum_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/BrunnianIsotypeExclusion.lean#L55-L63","doc":"**Key scalar identity.** The signs of the six permutations of `Fin 3` sum to\nzero: three even permutations contribute `+1`, three odd contribute `−1`.\n\nThis is the arithmetic crux behind the vanishing of the symmetric projection of\na totally antisymmetric tensor. ","signatureChunk":0}]}